979
01:01:00,340 --> 01:01:05,100
into the realm of continuous skill building and proactive prevention.

980
01:01:05,900 --> 01:01:07,140
Here's where it gets really interesting.

981
01:01:07,840 --> 01:01:12,150
The idea that we can actually prevent some of these conflicts from brewing in the first place.

982
01:01:12,290 --> 01:01:13,250
It's a powerful idea.

983
01:01:13,650 --> 01:01:22,560
It's about embedding these principles, not just as individual skills you learn in a workshop, but as core components of the organizational fabric, part of the company culture.

984
01:01:22,580 --> 01:01:23,660
So making it systemic.

985
01:01:23,880 --> 01:01:24,400
Exactly.

986
01:01:24,580 --> 01:01:30,020
And one significant part of this preventative approach focuses on empathy and perspective taking.

987
01:01:30,000 --> 01:01:30,520
Empathy.

988
01:01:30,660 --> 01:01:31,010
Okay.

989
01:01:31,050 --> 01:01:35,210
The sources indicate that misunderstandings often stem from a lacking emotional awareness.

990
01:01:35,690 --> 01:01:39,400
People just aren't tuning in to how others might be feeling or perceiving things.

991
01:01:39,580 --> 01:01:39,700
Right.

992
01:01:39,720 --> 01:01:41,000
We get stuck in our own heads.

993
01:01:41,360 --> 01:01:41,840
Precisely.

994
01:01:42,680 --> 01:01:48,510
What truly stood out in our sources about empathy training is its power to fundamentally shift perspective.

995
01:01:49,260 --> 01:01:50,600
It's not just about being nice.

996
01:01:51,260 --> 01:01:54,280
It's about equipping people to interpret others' actions differently.

997
01:01:55,240 --> 01:01:55,930
How so?

998
01:01:56,290 --> 01:02:00,080
Well, instead of assuming negative intent, you start considering other possibilities.

999
01:02:00,520 --> 01:02:01,480
Maybe they're under pressure.

1000
01:02:01,840 --> 01:02:03,080
Maybe there's miscommunication.

1001
01:02:03,640 --> 01:02:09,270
This subtle shift, the research shows, can lead to surprisingly dramatic reductions in workplace tension.

1002
01:02:09,670 --> 01:02:10,730
That's a crucial distinction.

1003
01:02:11,030 --> 01:02:14,340
It's about changing how we perceive others, not just how we react.

1004
01:02:14,580 --> 01:02:15,040
Exactly.

1005
01:02:15,520 --> 01:02:17,160
And it goes beyond just empathy training.

1006
01:02:17,480 --> 01:02:21,090
It also involves actively rotating roles within teams or departments.

1007
01:02:21,130 --> 01:02:22,080
Like job shadowing.

1008
01:02:22,100 --> 01:02:23,060
Sort of.

1009
