1936
01:55:39,110 --> 01:55:41,520
They can feel like walking through a minefield sometimes.

1937
01:55:41,580 --> 01:55:41,780
Yeah.

1938
01:55:42,060 --> 01:55:46,780
What's the key insight there for making them less confrontational?

1939
01:55:47,120 --> 01:55:49,390
Well, the big thing is clarity up front.

1940
01:55:49,410 --> 01:55:56,110
Being really clear about each party's needs and boundaries before you get into the haggling helps prevent that confrontational stuff later.

1941
01:55:56,590 --> 01:56:03,380
The sources even suggest using standardized negotiation templates sometimes just to keep discussions consistent and transparent.

1942
01:56:03,620 --> 01:56:04,140
Interesting.

1943
01:56:04,160 --> 01:56:07,910
And critically, always, always emphasizing mutual gain.

1944
01:56:07,890 --> 01:56:31,670
prompting negotiators to look for solutions where everyone benefits not just one side winning moving from i want x to how can we structure this so we both get what's most important to us finding the win-win exactly and using objective criteria helps anchor things in fairness things like market data if you're talking salary or agreed company policies if you're discussing project scope

1945
01:56:31,650 --> 01:56:33,570
It takes some of the personal demand out of it.

1946
01:56:33,650 --> 01:56:34,130
It makes sense.

1947
